## Generic Axis Lengths

Functions can use arrays with generic axis lengths by declaring generic arguments between `[]` after the function name to define the axis lengths.

For example: 
```
func add[A, B int](float32, [A][B]float32) [A][B]float32
```
defines an `add` function with two generic arguments, `A` and `B` of type `int`, and which takes two non-generic (runtime) arguments: a `float32` scalar, and an array of `float32` with two axes of generic lengths `A` and `B`. `add` returns an array with the same axis lengths.

The `add` function can then be called with different array shapes as in the example. In this example, `A` and `B` are automatically inferred by the compiler when calling `add`.
